 ## DevelopmentReadiness и readiness-гейт
 
+### Preparation Development Brief: current strict contract
+
+The implementation belongs to `sislex/sislexa-kanban`, not Core's `server.ts`.
+`apps/server/src/kanban/module.ts` owns the initial/recovery prompts, runtime
+schema and handler; `kanban/preparation.ts` owns complete-response parsing.
+Only one full JSON object with numeric `schemaVersion=2` is accepted. Only JSON
+whitespace may surround it. Duplicate decoded keys are rejected at every object
+level before the root object is constructed, including escaped spellings.
+Codex and Claude both validate the complete response, without selecting its last
+JSON message. Prefixes, suffixes, Markdown and multiple roots are rejected.
+
+Normalization follows parsing and only converts nonempty scalar string lists,
+exact boolean strings on supported flags, a nonempty scalar source ref,
+case/outer whitespace of canonical source statuses, and nonempty string-array
+component coverage to `{ required: [...] }`. It preserves `absent` and
+`unavailable`; it never infers missing requirements. String schema versions,
+kind aliases and unknown statuses are rejected. An optional
+`decisions[].questionId` must be omitted or a nonempty reference to a supplied
+question; null and invented links are rejected. Other valid nulls are preserved.
+All mandatory fields remain required. Non-none UI impact requires a required
+UI test, and every component requires nonempty coverage; a null Storybook id
+also requires concrete exclusion and alternative verification.
+
+`apps/server/src/taskPreparation.test.ts` markers TC-3 and TC-4 exercise the
+handler, prompt, field requirements, dependent UI constraints and normalization.
+Earlier historical nullable-link normalization and last-Codex-message extraction
+described below are superseded by this contract.
